<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coleraine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Coleraine is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-bann">River Bann</a> in County <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derry">Londonderry</a>, Northern Ireland. Mount Sandel nearby holds remains of one of the earliest known settlements in Ireland, about 9,000 years old. An Anglo-Norman castle stood there in the 13th century, and the town was rebuilt by the Irish Society of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">City of London</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plantation-of-ulster">Plantation of Ulster</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/coleraine.jpg" alt="Coleraine" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coleraine_Town_Hall.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
